      "description": "Review a rendered folio and publish it, or send it back with changes. Shared by every authoring process: authoring-a-document (this layer) and authoring-a-paper (folio-assistant-sci) call it after they validate and render, so review, publish and committee feedback are drawn once. What differs by folio kind stays with the caller: its writing loop, its own check (the content profile for a document, the Lean build for a paper), and its renderer. It ends one of three ways. `Published`: the caller closes its bean. `Changes asked` and `Feedback in: changes asked`: the caller goes back to its writing loop.",
      "enforcement": "advisory",
      "flowCount": 7,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/folio-assistant-core/directory/core-processes",
      "name": "Review and publish a folio",
